From: Oleg Nesterov <oleg@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:00:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] proc: use pid_has_task() in proc_inode_is_dead()

to make it more readable and consistent.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/atObuVZXbl9n-zFq@redhat.com
Signed-off-by: Oleg Nesterov <oleg@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Christian Brauner <brauner@kernel.org>
---
 fs/proc/base.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/proc/base.c b/fs/proc/base.c
index c9aebee0a338c..914b8964cbe4b 100644
--- a/fs/proc/base.c
+++ b/fs/proc/base.c
@@ -2065,7 +2065,7 @@ static int pid_revalidate(struct inode *dir, const struct qstr *name,
 
 static inline bool proc_inode_is_dead(struct inode *inode)
 {
-	return !proc_pid(inode)->tasks[PIDTYPE_PID].first;
+	return !pid_has_task(proc_pid(inode), PIDTYPE_PID);
 }
 
 int pid_delete_dentry(const struct dentry *dentry)
-- 
2.47.3

